SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Egypt's National Dialogue is for all forces except the faction that resorted to killing: Sisi","publisher":"Ahram Online / MENA","publication_date":"2022-07-04","url":"https://english.ahram.org.eg/News/471062.aspx","claim":"Sisi personally excluded the Muslim Brotherhood from the National Dialogue, characterizing the group as having chosen war and killing; the remarks stigmatized a broad opposition category but contained no express call for listeners to attack or punish its members.","locator":"HTML lines 47-58, 68-98","provisional_id":"WEB-3B-011","canonical_fact_key":"https://english.ahram.org.eg/News/471062.aspx|lines 47-58,68-98|Sisi excludes Brotherhood and characterizes it as choosing war and killing","disposition":"context","chapter_ids":["3B"],"methodology_ids":["3B.3","3B.5","3B.8"],"source_type":"state-aligned transcript-based news report","source_confidence":"high for words; medium for context","source_confidence_reason":"Contemporaneous report reproduces extended presidential remarks, but the full audiovisual transcript was not independently reviewed.","final_evidence_use":"context","period_fit":"Remarks were made in July 2022.","ruler_attribution":"Direct personal attribution.","contrary_evidence":["The government designated the Brotherhood a terrorist organization and cited historical violence as the reason for exclusion.","The remarks do not by themselves prove personal incitement to hatred or violence."],"lenses":["3B.3","3B.5","3B.8"]}

## Lens coverage and residual gaps

- **3B.1:** Strong adverse coverage: enforced disappearance, torture, political imprisonment, custodial death, and alleged extrajudicial killing. Gap: no complete nationwide denominator or verified presidential command chain.
- **3B.2:** Strong coverage of police, NSA, prison, and pro-military tribal-force abuse and weak accountability. Gap: incomplete military–tribal command records and no comprehensive prosecution dataset.
- **3B.3:** Searched directly in English and Arabic. Sisi used exclusionary security rhetoric about the Muslim Brotherhood, while state-aligned media used dehumanizing smears. **Residual gap:** no verified 2022 personal Sisi call for hatred, revenge, or physical violence.
- **3B.4:** Mixed coverage: prosecution/complaint and women-protection structures existed, pardons and releases occurred, but judicial orders were reportedly ignored and investigations lacked independence. Gap: no audited complaint-to-disposition data.
- **3B.5:** Strong adverse coverage of terrorism charges, surveillance, emergency courts, protest controls, and administrative restrictions. Gap: incomplete case-level testing of whether any specific security use was necessary and proportionate.
- **3B.6:** Evidence supports a broad political fear climate alongside continuing Sinai insurgent violence. Gap: no representative fear survey or comparable state-versus-nonstate victimization series.
- **3B.7:** Mixed evidence: real women-protection programs and church-fire response, but continuing violence against women, refugee abuse, religious discrimination, and an alleged child execution. Gap: sparse group-specific outcome data, especially disability, migrant, LGBT, and regional coverage.
- **3B.8:** Strong adverse coverage of COP27 arrests, surveillance, association restrictions, and retaliation. Pardons and dialogue were limited contrary evidence.
- **3B.9:** Mixed: rapid high-level response to the church fire, but preventive protest repression and alleged Sinai executions show coercive crisis responses. Gap: no complete after-action records for spontaneous disturbances.
- **3B.10:** Partial only. Target-year evidence establishes ongoing state repression and insurgent casualties, while some protection programs expanded. **Residual gap:** no methodologically comparable inherited-versus-year-end series covering political, communal, criminal, and preventable insecurity, so net safety change remains unresolved.

## Research accounting

- Documents discovered: **52**
- Underlying documents/pages opened or directly inspected: **20**
- Newly accepted source-claim units: **11**
- Reused evidence units verified: **8** — E003, E004, E005, E006, E007, E015, E036, E037
- Plausible documents rejected: **26**
- Access-blocked or fetch-failed: **6**
- Newly accepted organizations: **9**
- Source types: **6** — official presidential record, state-aligned reporting, international NGO investigation, domestic/specialist NGO reporting, intergovernmental program report, thematic press-freedom report

Rejected material principally consisted of wrong-year reports, search snippets without accessible underlying text, duplicative summaries, unattributed aggregation, and sources unable to distinguish state policy from personal presidential conduct. Blocked items included SIS pages returning 502 errors, the archived State Department human-rights page, the OHCHR communication download, and the USCIRF PDF.

## Cumulative manifest fallback

The managed workspace was read-only, and no filesystem-reading interface was available to retrieve or modify the existing `research-ledger-manifest.json`. The cumulative merge instruction therefore could not be executed safely without risking replacement of unseen prior entries. This fallback preserves every prior ID supplied in this turn and adds all new units:

